95 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 69 0 R
/T (This project presents the design and implementation of an E-Commerce and Inventory Management System backend built with Node.js, Express.js, MongoDB and Mongoose. The system lets customers browse products, maintain a shopping cart and place orders, lets sellers manage their own listings, stock levels and incoming orders, and gives administrators oversight of users, categories and overall order activity. )
/E (This project presents the design and implementation of an E-Commerce and Inventory Management System backend built with Node.js, Express.js, MongoDB and Mongoose. The system lets customers browse products, maintain a shopping cart and place orders, lets sellers manage their own listings, stock levels and incoming orders, and gives administrators oversight of users, categories and overall order activity. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
96 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 69 0 R
/T (The application exposes a RESTful API organised in an MVC-style layered architecture. Security is provided by bcrypt password hashing, JWT access and refresh tokens with refresh-token rotation, and role-based access control. Stock integrity is protected with atomic database updates so that stock can never become negative, even when several customers buy the same item at the same time. Four MongoDB aggregation pipelines generate sales, best-seller, inventory and order- status reports. Order and low-stock events are published through a Node.js EventEmitter and delivered to the right users in real time using Socket.IO. Payment is simulated and clearly flagged as such. The API was verified with a Postman collection of 87 requests covering success, validation, authentication, authorization, conflict and business-rule scenarios. )
/E (The application exposes a RESTful API organised in an MVC-style layered architecture. Security is provided by bcrypt password hashing, JWT access and refresh tokens with refresh-token rotation, and role-based access control. Stock integrity is protected with atomic database updates so that stock can never become negative, even when several customers buy the same item at the same time. Four MongoDB aggregation pipelines generate sales, best-seller, inventory and order- status reports. Order and low-stock events are published through a Node.js EventEmitter and delivered to the right users in real time using Socket.IO. Payment is simulated and clearly flagged as such. The API was verified with a Postman collection of 87 requests covering success, validation, authentication, authorization, conflict and business-rule scenarios. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
